  <h1>Delete Your Arokya Unavu Account</h1>

  <p>
    Arokya Unavu lets you request deletion of your account and the personal
    data associated with it at any time. Since account deletion is not yet
    available directly within the app, follow the steps below to submit a
    request.
  </p>

  <h2>How to request deletion</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Send an email to <a href="mailto:km.arasankpk266@gmail.com">km.arasankpk266@gmail.com</a>
        (or <a href="mailto:mutharasan.karuppaiyan@gmail.com">mutharasan.karuppaiyan@gmail.com</a>)
        from the email address associated with your Arokya Unavu account.</li>
    <li>Use the subject line: <strong>"Arokya Unavu — Account Deletion Request"</strong>.</li>
    <li>Include the name you used to sign up, so we can locate your account.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>We will confirm your identity and process the request within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account credentials (name, email address, and password) stored with our authentication provider (Firebase Authentication).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not affected</h2>
  <p>
    Arokya Unavu's recipe, food, and remedy content is shared app-wide and is
    not tied to your individual account, so deleting your account does not
    affect this content. We do not currently store any other personal data
    (such as saved favorites) on our servers — that information, if any,
    exists only on your device and is removed when you uninstall the app.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Retention:</strong> After deletion, your account data is
    permanently removed from our systems within 30 days and is not recoverable.
  </div>

  <p>
    Questions about this process? Contact us at
    <a href="mailto:km.arasankpk266@gmail.com">km.arasankpk266@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>

